{"_meta":{"source":"Yahoo Finance via yfinance (profile, statements, analyst estimates)","fetched_at":"2026-10-23T15:56:36+00:00","status":"ok","error":null,"last_success":"2026-10-23T15:56:36+00:00"},"data":{"profile":{"name":"Carl Zeiss Meditec AG","sector":"Healthcare","industry":"Medical Instruments & Supplies","country":"Germany","city":"Jena","website":"https://www.zeiss.com/meditec-ag/de/investor-relations.html?vaURL=www.zeiss.de/meditec-ag/ir","employees":5784,"summary":"Carl Zeiss Meditec AG operates as a medical technology company in Germany, rest of Europe, North America, and Asia. It operates in two segments, Ophthalmology and Microsurgery. The Ophthalmology segment offers products and solutions for the diagnosis and treatment of chronic eye diseases, including slit lamps, refractometers, and tonometers; optical coherence tomography and fundus cameras for retina examination; functional glaucoma diagnostic devices (perimeters); surgical ophthalmology products comprising surgical microscopes, biometers, and phacoemulsification and vitrectomy equipment; intraocular lenses for cataract surgery; and systems and consumables for laser eye surgery that include the VISUMAX femtosecond laser, which enables minimally invasive correction of vision defects using lenticular extraction, as well as digital products for the storage, analysis, and sharing of clinical data. The Microsurgery segment provides products and solutions for minimally invasive surgical treatments, including surgical visualization, interoperative radiotherapy, interoperative pathology, special surgical instruments, and digital solutions, as well as the ZEISS Tumor Workflow, a cross-product workflow solution. It serves physicians in various fields and hospitals. The company has a strategic collaboration with Envision Health Technologies Inc. to help advance glaucoma care through gamified virtual reality technology. The company was founded in 1846 and is headquartered in Jena, Germany. Carl Zeiss Meditec AG operates as a subsidiary of ZEISS Group.","exchange":"XETRA","currency":"EUR","financial_currency":"EUR","summary_fr":"Carl Zeiss Meditec AG opère en tant que société de technologie médicale en Allemagne, dans le reste de l'Europe, en Amérique du Nord et en Asie. Elle opère en deux segments, l’ophtalmologie et la microchirurgie. Le segment Ophthalmologie propose des produits et des solutions pour le diagnostic et le traitement des maladies oculaires chroniques, y compris les lampes à fente, les réfractomètres et les tonomètres; tomographie par cohérence optique et caméras fundus pour l'examen de la rétine; dispositifs de diagnostic du glaucome fonctionnel (périmètres); produits de stockage ophtalmologique chirurgical comprenant des microscopes chirurgicaux, des biomètres et des équipements de vitrectomie."},"valuation":{"market_cap_yahoo":3111032320,"shares_outstanding":87536079,"trailing_pe":25.568346,"forward_pe":24.344467,"price_to_book":1.4823775,"ev_to_ebitda":16.506,"ev_to_revenue":1.648,"dividend_yield":0.0161,"payout_ratio":0.3957,"beta_yahoo":1.326},"targets":{"current_price":35.54,"mean":26.92667,"median":26.5,"high":35.0,"low":18.1,"n_analysts":15,"reco_mean":3.73333,"reco_key":"underperform"},"calendar":{"earnings_dates":["2026-08-06"],"eps_avg":0.47667,"eps_low":0.37,"eps_high":0.59,"revenue_avg":618984300,"ex_dividend":"2026-03-27","dividend_date":null},"holders":{"insiders_pct":0.59138,"institutions_pct":0.19881001,"institutions_float_pct":0.48654,"institutions_n":174,"institutions":[{"name":"Gilder, Gagnon, Howe & Co.","pct":0.0001,"shares":11744,"value":417381,"date":"2023-06-30","chg":1.0}],"funds":[{"name":"AIM Intl Mutual Fd.s -Invesco Intl Small-Mid Company Fd.","pct":0.0074,"shares":646922,"value":22991608,"date":"2026-07-31","chg":-0.13260001},{"name":"VANGUARD STAR FUNDS-Vanguard Total International Stock Index Fund","pct":0.0058,"shares":510318,"value":18136702,"date":"2026-07-31","chg":-0.0109},{"name":"VANGUARD TAX-MANAGED FUNDS-Va